# A struct literal at a disjunctive target mixing a plain field with
# conditional ones: which alternative the instance's struct is depends on
# which arms hold, so it is matched to none.
-- source.cue --
k: "a" | "b"
-- target.cue --
o: {branch: 1, one: string} | {branch: 2, two: string}
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {
	o: {
		branch: 1
		if v0_0.k == "a" {one: "x"}
		if v0_0.k == "b" {one: "y"}
	}
}
-- out --
unknown
v1_0.o is a struct written to v1_0.o, a disjunction in the target schema, mixing fields with conditional fields or embeddings, so which alternative it is an instance of depends on the instance; write it as one struct per alternative, each with its fields unconditional, in its own arm (rule unknown-target-constraint) @ lens.cue:3:2
